  <data name="Label1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Borrow up to 3 books at a time.
• Select the books you want to borrow.
• Borrow Date is today.
• Due Date is 2 days after borrowing.
• Click Borrow to confirm.
• Click Clear to remove your selections.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Label6.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• View the books you borrowed.
• Select the books to return.
• Click Return to submit them.
• The librarian will inspect the books before 
completing the return.
• Click Clear to remove your selections.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Label17.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How many books can I borrow?
A: You can borrow a maximum of 3 books at a time.

When should I return my borrowed books?
A: Books must be returned within 2 days from the borrow date 
to avoid overdue penalties.

Why is my returned book still marked as "Pending"?
A: The librarian must inspect the book's condition before the 
return is confirmed.

How do I pay my penalty?
A: Pay the penalty at the cashier, then upload your payment 
receipt through the system for librarian verification.

Why should I log out after using the system?
A: Logging out helps protect your account and prevents 
unauthorized access, especially when using a shared computer.

Can I borrow another book if I already have 3 borrowed books?
A: No. You must return at least one book before borrowing another.

What happens if I return a book late?
A: An overdue penalty will be automatically calculated and added 
to your account.

What happens if my borrowed book is damaged or lost?
A: The librarian will assess the book's condition and the corresponding 
penalty will be applied based on the library's policy.</value>
